  nonce: 4ad8  # 4ad8
  message: "Might an analogous issue affect other hypergumbo-supported languages?"  # 4ad8
- op: discuss  # 6809
  at: '2026-03-07T22:16:40Z'  # 6809
  by: agent  # 6809
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6809
  clock: 5  # 6809
  nonce: '6809'  # 6809
  message: "Yes, structural interface/protocol matching could affect other languages. Java/Kotlin have nominal typing (explicit implements), so they're fine. But TypeScript uses structural typing like Go — a class satisfying an interface's shape is compatible without explicit implements. Rust traits require explicit impl blocks, so they're covered. Python protocols (typing.Protocol) are structural — similar gap possible. Swift protocols require explicit conformance. Ruby duck-typing is implicit but we don't track implements edges for Ruby. Net: TypeScript and Python Protocol are the two analogous gaps. Will create tracker items."  # 6809
